WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:15.635
Later Mowgli returned to the cave.

2
00:00:15.636 --> 00:00:21.108
Mother Wolf sensed something was wrong. "What is it, son?"

3
00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:24.971
Mowgli didn't want to tell her about the other wolves.

4
00:00:24.972 --> 00:00:29.268
"Oh, some bat was chattering about Shere Khan.

5
00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:34.592
He's hunting nearby, so I think I'll hunt near the people's fields tonight."

6
00:00:34.593 --> 00:00:40.361
With that, Mowgli hurried away, racing downward through the bushes.

7
00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:47.958
Near the stream at the bottom of the valley, he heard howls.

8
00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:51.297
The wolves were hunting.

9
00:00:51.298 --> 00:00:54.666
"Spring, Akela!" a young wolf shouted.

10
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:59.689
"Show your strength!"

11
00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.522
Mowgli heard teeth snapping and then a yelp.

12
00:01:03.523 --> 00:01:08.227
Akela had sprung at something—and missed.

13
00:01:08.228 --> 00:01:15.025
Mowgli raced on toward the village.

14
00:01:15.026 --> 00:01:21.147
Mowgli had never come this close to the village before.

15
00:01:21.148 --> 00:01:26.267
He slipped over to a hut and peered inside.

16
00:01:26.268 --> 00:01:30.039
A red flower glowed along one wall.

17
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.461
He watched a woman get up and blow on it.

18
00:01:33.462 --> 00:01:37.295
Then she fed it some sticks.

19
00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:40.184
Mowgli sighed.

20
00:01:40.185 --> 00:01:46.101
The red flower was dangerous. What should he do?

21
00:01:46.102 --> 00:01:49.641
He waited through the night.

22
00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:54.607
In the morning he saw a child pick up a pot.

23
00:01:54.608 --> 00:01:59.302
The boy filled it with lumps of the red-hot flower.

24
00:01:59.303 --> 00:02:02.050
Mowgli laughed.

25
00:02:02.051 --> 00:02:10.759
"That small cub can handle the red flower," he thought. "So can I!"

26
00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.956
He ran at the boy and grabbed the pot.

27
00:02:14.957 --> 00:02:19.573
Then he ran deep into the jungle.

28
00:02:19.574 --> 00:02:28.103
After some time he stopped to blow at the red stuff as the woman had done.

29
00:02:28.104 --> 00:02:30.812
"Now it's time to feed it."

30
00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:34.508
He dropped twigs and bark on the red flower.

31
00:02:34.509 --> 00:02:37.709
It quickly bloomed again.

32
00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:42.051
Mowgli grinned. "I did it!"

33
00:02:42.052 --> 00:02:45.655
Halfway up the hill he met Bagheera.

34
00:02:45.656 --> 00:02:47.951
The panther looked worried.

35
00:02:47.952 --> 00:02:50.651
"Akela failed at last night's hunt.

36
00:02:50.652 --> 00:02:55.766
The wolves wanted to kill him, but they were looking for you instead."

37
00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.440
"I was in the valley.

38
00:02:57.441 --> 00:03:04.022
I am ready to fight now." Mowgli held up the fire pot.

39
00:03:04.023 --> 00:03:06.515
Bagheera nodded. "Good."

40
00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:09.976
Then he peered more closely at the red flower.

41
00:03:09.977 --> 00:03:14.897
"Are you afraid of that thing? It's dangerous when it blooms."

42
00:03:14.898 --> 00:03:22.682
Mowgli shrugged. "I'm not afraid. In fact, I remember it from long ago.

43
00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:32.101
Before I was a wolf, I rested near the red flower. It was warm and pleasant."

44
00:03:32.102 --> 00:03:35.953
That night Mowgli headed to the pack council.

45
00:03:35.954 --> 00:03:41.360
He stayed in the back so the wolves wouldn't see the fire pot.

46
00:03:41.361 --> 00:03:44.758
Mowgli gulped when he saw the empty rock.

47
00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:49.155
Akela lay beside it, injured from the hunt.

48
00:03:49.156 --> 00:03:53.104
The pack was removing him as leader!

49
00:03:53.105 --> 00:03:59.395
Shere Khan walked around the rock, young wolves trailing him.

50
00:03:59.396 --> 00:04:04.361
When everyone had gathered, Shere Khan began to speak.

51
00:04:04.362 --> 00:04:10.075
"He has no right to speak here!" Bagheera whispered furiously to Mowgli.

52
00:04:10.076 --> 00:04:13.922
Mowgli sprang to his feet. "Why is he—"

53
00:04:13.923 --> 00:04:18.165
"Quiet, man cub!" some wolves yelled.

54
00:04:18.166 --> 00:04:21.204
Akela slowly raised his head.

55
00:04:21.205 --> 00:04:23.676
"I'm weak and old.

56
00:04:23.677 --> 00:04:28.984
Another wolf must fight me to become the pack's new leader."

57
00:04:28.985 --> 00:04:34.903
There was a long silence. None wanted to fight Akela.

58
00:04:34.904 --> 00:04:39.755
"I want only the man cub," Shere Khan roared.

59
00:04:39.756 --> 00:04:44.864
"Give me the man cub, and I will leave your pack alone."

60
00:04:44.865 --> 00:04:52.795
"Let the tiger take Mowgli!" a wolf yelled. "Mowgli is not a wolf!"

61
00:04:52.796 --> 00:04:55.342
Akela lifted his head again.

62
00:04:55.343 --> 00:04:59.408
"Mowgli has eaten our food and slept with us.

63
00:04:59.409 --> 00:05:04.770
He has not broken the law of the jungle. He's our brother."

64
00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:12.263
"No, he's a man!" the pack snarled. Shere Khan's tail flicked.

65
00:05:12.264 --> 00:05:16.576
Bagheera glanced at Mowgli. "Now!"

66
00:05:16.577 --> 00:05:21.736
Mowgli stood upright—showing the fire pot to the pack.

67
00:05:21.737 --> 00:05:25.338
"You've often told me that I am not a wolf.

68
00:05:25.339 --> 00:05:30.264
So I won't call you my sisters and brothers anymore!"

69
00:05:30.265 --> 00:05:33.520
He flung the fire pot on the ground.

70
00:05:33.521 --> 00:05:39.369
Swiftly it bloomed into furious flames.
